# What C64PINE needs, per package manager. One line per need:
#   GROUP | WHAT | apt (Debian, Ubuntu, Mint ...) | pacman (Arch, Manjaro ...) | dnf (Fedora, RHEL, Rocky, Alma ...) | apk (Alpine)
# Several names = all of them. "a/b" = a, or else b. "src:NAME" = build it from source into ~/.c64pine/opt (the recipe is
# src/NAME.sh), when no package of it is installed or installable. "-" = not available there (that part is left out).
# Groups: core = needed; build = only for building (the uninstaller can remove them); the rest are optional parts.
core|X11, xinit and the X tools|xserver-xorg-core xinit xauth x11-xserver-utils x11-xkb-utils x11-utils|xorg-server xorg-xinit xorg-xauth xorg-xrdb xorg-xset xorg-xsetroot xorg-xrandr xorg-setxkbmap xorg-xprop xorg-xdpyinfo|xorg-x11-server-Xorg xorg-x11-xinit xorg-x11-xauth xrdb xset xsetroot xrandr setxkbmap xprop xdpyinfo|xorg-server xinit xauth xrdb xset xsetroot xrandr setxkbmap xprop xdpyinfo
core|Openbox (the window manager)|openbox|openbox|openbox|openbox
core|xdotool, D-Bus for X|xdotool dbus-x11|xdotool dbus|xdotool dbus-x11|xdotool dbus-x11
core|fonts, curl, jq, xdg-utils, ALSA tools|fonts-dejavu-core curl jq xdg-utils alsa-utils|ttf-dejavu curl jq xdg-utils alsa-utils|dejavu-sans-mono-fonts curl jq xdg-utils alsa-utils|font-dejavu curl jq xdg-utils alsa-utils
